# Scenario: software programme office analyses a delayed regulatory reporting release.
fishbone "Regulatory reporting release delay"

effect "Release missed the statutory deadline"

category people "People"
category process "Process"
category platform "Platform"
category partners "Partners"

people: "Two analysts reassigned"
  - "Backfill approved after code freeze"
people: "One expert owns the reporting rules"
people: "QA lead on leave through UAT"
people: "Team split across three workstreams"

process: "Requirements changed after build started"
  - "Approval gate skipped"
process: "Scope added mid-sprint without trade-off"
process: "Estimates never revised after discovery"
process: "Defects triaged weekly, not daily"
process: "Regulatory sign-off queued behind an audit"

platform: "Test environment unstable"
  - "Masked production data unavailable"
platform: "Deploy pipeline shared with another release"
platform: "Report times out on the full dataset"
platform: "Schema migration blocked by a legacy job"

partners: "Vendor interface specification arrived late"
  - "Two revisions after the freeze"
partners: "Vendor test window limited to weekdays"
partners: "Change order took six weeks to sign"
partners: "Regulator clarification still pending"
